{"name":"Engagement Silver","hex":"#c2c6c0","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"engagement","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An appointment, especially to speak or perform.","Connection or attachment."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/engagement"},{"term":"silver","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A lustrous, white, metallic element, atomic number 47, atomic weight 107.87, symbol Ag.","Coins made from silver or any similar white metal."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Made from silver.","Made from another white metal."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/silver"}],"entries":[{"title":"Engagement","blocks":[{"text":"An engagement or betrothal is the period of time between the declaration of acceptance of a marriage proposal and the marriage itself. During this period, a couple is said to be fiancés, \"betrothed\", \"intended\", \"affianced\", \"engaged to be married\", or simply \"engaged\". Future brides and grooms may be called fiancée (feminine) or fiancé (masculine), \"the betrothed\", \"wife-to-be\" or \"husband-to-be\", respectively. The duration of the courtship varies vastly, and is largely dependent on cultural norms or upon the agreement of the parties involved."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/11/William-Adolphe_Bouguereau_%281825-1905%29_-_The_Proposal_%281872%29.jpg/330px-William-Adolphe_Bouguereau_%281825-1905%29_-_The_Proposal_%281872%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Engagement","wikidata":"Q157512"},{"title":"Silver","blocks":[{"text":"Silver is a chemical element; it has symbol Ag and atomic number 47. A soft, white, lustrous transition metal, it exhibits the highest electrical conductivity, thermal conductivity and reflectivity of any metal. Silver is found in the Earth's crust in the pure, free elemental form, as an alloy with gold (electrum) and other metals, and in minerals such as acanthite, argentite and chlorargyrite. Most silver is recovered as a byproduct of lead–zinc, copper and gold mining and refining."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/55/Silver_crystal.jpg/330px-Silver_crystal.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Silver","wikidata":"Q1090"},{"title":"Silver (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Silver or metallic gray is a color tone resembling gray that is a representation of the color of polished silver."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/de/Clemens_Friedell_silver_centerpiece_bowl_top_view_-_HLABG.png/330px-Clemens_Friedell_silver_centerpiece_bowl_top_view_-_HLABG.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Silver_(color)","wikidata":"Q317802"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1e/Engagement_gifts_basket_%2801%29.jpg/500px-Engagement_gifts_basket_%2801%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1e/Engagement_gifts_basket_%2801%29.jpg/1280px-Engagement_gifts_basket_%2801%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1e/Engagement_gifts_basket_%2801%29.jpg/500px-Engagement_gifts_basket_%2801%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Modern engagement gifts basket in Bangladesh.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AEngagement_gifts_basket_(01).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0f/Lionel_Logue_1906.jpg/500px-Lionel_Logue_1906.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0f/Lionel_Logue_1906.jpg/500px-Lionel_Logue_